\begin{abstract}
We present a unified mathematical formulation of the National Infrastructure
Simulation Stress Test Protocol. The protocol consists of four execution phases:
ingest saturation, thermodynamic substrate shock, sovereign kernel fault injection,
and zero-knowledge audit. Each phase contributes a distinct operator to the
evolution of the encrypted state tensor $\Psi(x,t)$ defined on the simulation
manifold $\Omega$. We derive the governing equations, stability metrics, invariant
conditions, and cryptographic--astrophysical coupling terms relevant to the
sovereign simulation architecture.
\end{abstract}

